          "unit": "rise_in_12",
          "kind": "measured",
          "note": "Lower than the colonial American norm, because slate and lead permit it and because the roof is frequently concealed."
        },
        "parapet_conceals_roof": {
          "value": true,
          "unit": "none",
          "kind": "measured",
          "note": "The 1707 and 1709 London Building Acts drove the parapet by outlawing the projecting eaves cornice in timber. A code decision that became the defining fact of the London elevation."
        }
      },
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rule": "Steep by later standards and shallower than the medieval work it replaced: the English Georgian roof is hidden behind a parapet in town and expressed in the country.",
